# Project
This is a new project. It will have 3 subprojects a widget-backend and a widget-frontend and a host-frontend. Create these folders.

## The widget:
It is a fastapi+webcomponent based widget demonstrating connectivity and CORS.

### The widget-backend
is a simple python fastapi app with 
- an api endpoint of "/echo", accepting post json and replying with the same data.
- a "/chat-echo" endpoint which is a websocket endpoint that also echoes every message received

### The widget frontend
is a webcomponent app, based on typescript and webpack
It provides a web component that calls the echo service with a fixed message of "Hello" demonstrating connectivity.
And a simple input area with a send button (also accepting ctrl-enter for send). A websocket should be created upon webcomponent loading and the area should be made active.

The frontend is rendered as a hovering div in the lower right corner with a fixed size and vertical scroll bar for the message history.

The widget frontend code is served by the widget backend app after building and copying into a dist folder in the widget backend

## Host frontend
is a web application where index.html pulls in the bundle of the webcomponent and includes the widget.
The app can have a simple javascript source as well, so that future interactions, such as events can be handled.

## Docs
Provide instructions on running each project.
To demonstrate cors, provide a means to run the host independent of the widget.

## Tech
- use uv and pyproject.toml
- use py type hints
- add ruff as dev dependency and add instructions on how to use
- test the py code w/ ruff
- create a helper script to build and run all, run-all.sh
- test the process by running the run-all.sh
- add .gitignore w usual exemptions, also exclude lock files
